                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Competent and cheap \"Match 3\" gameplay marred by lack of polish, poor translation, and bugs.\n\nThe first issue you may run into is that assets for the female character models will fail to load so you will have to find and download the uncensored version of said assets (whether you want to or not) just to get something to show up other than a purple outline. Confused? Just search the game's discussion board for the word \"purple\".\n\nSmall bugs abound such as a mismatch between your mouse cursor placement on the screen and what location it's activating in-game. This forced me to stop playing in full screen because I'd often mis-click the gems I wanted to move.\n\nThe boobies themselves are OK. More on the level of art from 2000s with only the weakest attempts at variety in titilating the player or any kind of spice.\nThere's over a hundred achievements to earn and they're all fairly easy to get if that's your bag though.\n\nThe money required for upgrades is insanely high so I just ended up editing my save file to give me a few hundred thousand gold to empty out the shop. This actually didn't do much to destroy end-game difficulty as the final opponents have a big HP pool and you are limited by not only your own health but the number of turns you can take to defeat any one of them.\n\nSo was there anything good?\nYeah, the \"match 3\" part was actually great! You need to actually pay attention to the board and try to set up 4 or 5 gem combos ahead of time to win in the allotted number of turns. Pulling off those 3 S-Gem combos (or the rare 4 S-Gem combo) and watching the big BADABOOM was always satisfying as it almost always either won you the game or put the opponent on her last legs.\n\nI got my money's worth from the game, but if you're expecting a AAA polished experience, amazing drawings, or great storyline then you're better off with something else.",
